From: yinjiayi <yinjiayi@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Defer executable stripping to RPM post-processing

Retain the original targets and compiler/link rule. RPM needs the unstripped
binary for normal debug products. Downstream-only, MIT; remove when upstream
supports packaging-controlled stripping. No upstream write.

--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -27 +27 @@
-	@strip $@
+	# Final stripping is performed by the RPM packaging scripts.
